cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use oxihipo in work that leads to a publication, please cite it."
title: "oxihipo: a Rust reader and writer for the HIPO v6 container, with a columnar Python binding"
abstract: >-
  oxihipo reads and writes the HIPO v6 binary container used at Jefferson Lab
  CLAS12. The Rust core streams records with bounded memory; the Python binding
  presents banks as columnar, uproot-shaped Awkward arrays built zero-copy from
  buffers filled with the GIL released.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ouillon
    given-names: Mathieu
repository-code: "https://github.com/mathieuouillon/oxihipo"
url: "https://mathieuouillon.github.io/oxihipo/"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
keywords:
  - HIPO
  - CLAS12
  - Jefferson Lab
  - nuclear physics
  - columnar I/O
  - Awkward Array
  - Rust
